# UI (dingoConfig copy)

Enforcer: `dotnet test ui\tests\CustomPdm.Tests` (unit + live sim), mutation runs in each job; none yet for the rest.

- The UI treats A1, A2 and B as ONE PDM: settings are made on `/pdm`; per-board editing only on the Advanced screen, through the conflict engine ("X is already assigned to Y. Overwrite?") (Dan, 2026-11-16).
- Critical settings (base IDs, CAN bit rate, critical temperature, fan exempt mask) change only through the unlock + type-the-value + confirm dialog.
- Stock dingoConfig files: change as little as possible, mark each change `// custom-pdm:`; new code in new files under `domain/CustomPdm` and `web/Components/CustomPdm`.
- Live sim test classes need `[Collection("sim")]` (else `SlcanBridgeTests` fails in parallel). Run live tests against a sim `.so` built from the same firmware as the branch.
- Never stop Dan's play app (main checkout, port 5000) or its bridge (port 3333); start your own app with `-- --urls http://localhost:<port>` and your own bridge port and `.so` copy.
- Never write one board's sensor temperature limits onto another board: PdmThermal converts the one hot-spot set per board; a board without a thermal model keeps its own factory limits (ADR-2026-11-21-temp-onepdm-ui).
- A /pdm panel picks its board through `PdmView.RoleOr` (never a hard-coded board name): other open tabs can see a half-built PDM (Never do: the Values panel defaulted to board B and crashed every other tab on New PDM, 2026-11-21). Panel tests use bUnit.
